    "body": "This speeds up `vim.json.encode()` and `vim.json.decode()` for the shapes common in LSP and JSON-RPC traffic: small objects, short arrays, integers, plain strings, and bare `:`/`,` separators.\n\n## Changes\n\n- encode: write integral numbers without `snprintf()`\n- decode: parse plain integers without `strtoll()`\n- decode: return strings without escapes as a slice of the input\n- encode: write strings straight into the reserved buffer\n- decode: consume `:` and `,` without a token\n- decode: pre-size small tables, but only after the first token shows the container is non-empty\n- decode: keep the escaped-string loop state in locals\n\nEvery fast path falls back to the existing code on anything unusual, so error messages, character positions, and output stay the same.\n\n## Benchmarks\n\nPlain Release build, `lua_cjson.c` is the only difference between the two binaries. Same-path A/B, shuffled rounds, medians. A byte-identical control binary measured 0.993x/0.989x, so the noise is about 1%.\n\nLSP-like payload (118 KB, 2000 generated objects with `id`, `name`, `tags`, `ok`), 15 rounds:\n\n| | before | after | ratio |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| encode | 603.7 us | 414.1 us | 0.686 |\n| decode | 692.7 us | 464.1 us | 0.670 |\n\nAdditional decode payloads, 15 rounds:\n\n| payload | before | after | ratio |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| pretty (233 KB) | 734.0 us | 525.5 us | 0.716 |\n| escapes (99 KB) | 106.9 us | 73.3 us | 0.686 |\n| 100k `{}` | 5730.3 us | 5398.8 us | 0.942 |\n| 100k `[]` | 4298.5 us | 3871.8 us | 0.901 |\n\nThe payloads are generated, not captured from a real LSP session; real traces will vary with their message mix. Absolute times differ between runs because of machine load; the ratios are stable.\n\nInstruction counts for the compact payload: encode -27.6%, decode -33.3% (`perf stat`, `instructions:u`).\n\nThe pretty, escapes, and empty payloads are miss cases for some fast paths. They are included to show the checks are not a net drag; all are at parity or faster.\n\n## Correctness\n\n- `test/functional/lua/json_spec.lua`: 20/20\n- `test/functional/vimscript/json_functions_spec.lua`: 76/76\n- encode, decode, and comment corpora byte-identical to the base\n- escape corpus byte-identical, including error messages and character positions\n- `clang-format` clean\n\n## Notes\n\n- The table pre-size is a heuristic: four hash slots for objects and four array slots for arrays. Empty containers use `lua_newtable()` and pay nothing.\n- The string fast path scans for `\"`, `\\`, and NUL. Strings with escapes use the copying path, which now keeps the input and output pointers in locals.\n- No build system or dependency changes.\n\nAI-assisted\n",
