        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "Sorry, I misread that as a verdict rather than a question.\n\nAgreed on the plan: upstream first, port it back here, then decide what to add on top.\n\nSome of this is worth sending upstream, and I do want to propose it there -- the integer fast paths, the string fast paths, and the `:`/`,` handling are generic and don't depend on Neovim.\n\nThere are also Neovim/LSP-specific pieces, though, such as the heuristic that reserves 4 hash/array slots for small tables, which is tuned for JSON-RPC messages. I doubt lua-cjson would take that, so I'd keep it Neovim-side for now and revisit it after the upstream work lands.\n",
